---
/**
 * What players ask before they play: how to get it running, how it battles,
 * trading and saves. A menu window of questions with the ▶ cursor on the one
 * that's open, its answer printed under it. Native disclosure widgets, so it
 * works without JavaScript and every answer is in the page for search and
 * screen readers.
 */
import Place from "~/components/route/Place.astro"
import { PATCHER_URL, REPOSITORY_URL } from "~/lib/content"
import { RELEASE_LABEL } from "~/lib/release"
---

<Place id="faq" popup="fall" name="QUESTIONS" title="Before you set out." grass={[4, 5]}>
  <div class="faq-menu gba-window gba-text window-links mt-8 grid max-w-3xl gap-[calc(4*var(--px))] [--px:2px]">
    <details class="faq" name="faq" open>
      <summary>How do I play it?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Wayfarer comes as a .ups patch. Apply it to your own Pokémon Emerald (U) ROM, for example
          with <a href={PATCHER_URL}>Rom Patcher JS</a> in your browser, and play the patched ROM in an
          emulator. The patch doesn't include the game itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq" name="faq">
      <summary>Which emulators work?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Any up-to-date emulator that runs ROM hacks. These are known to work:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><span class="faq-term">PC and Mac:</span> mGBA</li>
          <li><span class="faq-term">Android:</span> Pizza Boy, Lemuroid, or RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
          <li><span class="faq-term">iOS:</span> Delta, Ignited, or RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
          <li><span class="faq-term">Linux handhelds:</span> RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq" name="faq">
      <summary>How does it battle?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          With modern mechanics: the physical and special split, and updated stats, types and moves. TMs
          are reusable, so teach them as often as you like.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq" name="faq">
      <summary>Can I trade and battle with friends?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Trades and battles over the GBA link work, with a link cable or your emulator's link play.
          The GameCube, e-Reader and Berry Fix extras are gone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq" name="faq">
      <summary>Will my save carry over to updates?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>From v1.0 on, yes. Updates after that keep your save.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq" name="faq">
      <summary>Is it free?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Wayfarer is a free fan game, and you can follow every change
          <a href={REPOSITORY_URL}>on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq" name="faq">
      <summary>When does it come out?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          On {RELEASE_LABEL}. <a href="/wayfarer-release.ics" download>Add it to your calendar</a>, or leave your
          email with Professor Oak and he'll write when it's out.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</Place>

<style>
  .faq summary {
    display: flex;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The menu cursor, on the open question and on the one under the pointer. */
  .faq summary::before {
    content: "";
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: calc(10 * var(--px));
  }

  .faq[open] summary::before,
  .faq summary:hover::before,
  .faq summary:focus-visible::before {
    content: "▶";
  }

  .faq summary:focus-visible,
  .faq-term {
    outline: none;
    color: var(--color-ink-blue);
    text-shadow:
      var(--dot) 0 var(--color-ink-blue-shadow),
      0 var(--dot) var(--color-ink-blue-shadow),
      var(--dot) var(--dot) var(--color-ink-blue-shadow);
  }

  /* The answer, set in under its question the way the game indents a submenu. */
  .faq-answer {
    margin: calc(4 * var(--px)) 0 calc(8 * var(--px)) calc(10 * var(--px));
    padding-left: calc(8 * var(--px));
    border-left: var(--px) solid var(--color-ink-shadow);
  }

  .faq-answer ul {
    margin-top: calc(4 * var(--px));
  }

  .faq-answer li::before {
    content: "· ";
  }
</style>
